                <pb facs="0155" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/686: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-27T23:00:00-04:00">August 27, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>775. Your 936, August 13, 1 p.m. The Department has found your telegram under
                    reference most helpful. The Department transmitted the substance to the War
                    Department and the War Department has stated that the views expressed by you in
                    regard to the potentialities of an American air force in China coincide with the
                    views held by that Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
